   "source": [
    "# MARKERS"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "76923ff8-5d2d-4f4e-b1b0-7db6e54fd98c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "What is a marker?\n",
    "A marker is a small symbol placed at each data point on your line.\n",
    "\n",
    "Why are markers useful?\n",
    "Markers make it easier to see where the actual observations are.\n",
    "\n",
    "common markers :-\n",
    "\"o\" → circle\n",
    "\"s\" → square\n",
    "\"^\" → triangle\n",
    "\"*\" → star\n",
    "\n",
    "syntax = ax.plot(x, y, marker=\"o\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 130,
