  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c51c2ddb-82aa-4acd-9463-91f02748e9d1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Transparency"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "e3831e6d-cc00-4a10-b1ec-f11dbc2da04d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "What is transparency?\n",
    "Sometimes a line or marker can cover other information. Matplotlib lets us make it partly transparent using alpha.\n",
    "\n",
    "alpha = 0.5\n",
    "0 → completely transparent\n",
    "1 → completely solid\n",
    "\n",
    "syntax = ax.plot(x, y, color=\"blue\", alpha=0.5)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 134,
   "id": "c19cb611-8e75-43ae-b680-b7b8daf09903",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "fig,ax = plt.subplots()\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.plot([10, 20, 30, 40, 50], [25, 18, 30, 22, 35],\n",
    "       color = \"blue\",\n",
    "       alpha = 0.5\n",
    "       )\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"W-Shape line chart\")\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"X\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Y\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6b1a9df5-add5-4db4-9ac6-d62214f91624",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Grid"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "e6fc4852-d894-4a62-96ea-06429e110566",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Why use a grid?\n",
    "A grid adds horizontal and/or vertical reference lines behind the chart.\n",
    "    \n",
    "It helps the reader estimate values more easily."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 135,
   "id": "4b2952dd-df1a-468b-a9f7-3244bf250024",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "fig,ax = plt.subplots()\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.plot([10, 20, 30, 40, 50], [25, 18, 30, 22, 35],\n",
    "       color = \"green\",\n",
    "       linestyle = \"-.\",\n",
    "       linewidth = 2,\n",
    "       marker = \"*\",\n",
    "       markersize = 15,\n",
    "       markerfacecolor = \"red\",\n",
    "       markeredgecolor = \"black\",\n",
    "       )\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"W-Shape line chart\")\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"X\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Y\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.grid()\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d67a7b52-9d7f-4a92-97d1-c4d1e14a5a42",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "## Multiple Lines and Legend"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "358bea64-5046-4c97-87f7-b081666e5c39",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Why do we need a legend?\n",
    "Suppose a chart has two or more lines.\n",
    "The reader needs to know which line represents which data.\n",
    "A legend provides that information."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 136,
   "id": "2b5bf121-3cfb-46dd-b5f5-fad12a65e3c5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "fig,ax = plt.subplots()\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.plot([1, 2, 3, 4, 5], [10, 15, 12, 20, 18],\n",
    "        label = \"Sales\",\n",
    "        marker = \"*\",\n",
    "        markersize = 10,\n",
    "        markerfacecolor = \"red\")\n",
    "ax.plot([1, 2, 3, 4, 5],[15, 18, 20, 25,23],\n",
    "        label = \"Profit\",\n",
    "        marker = \"o\",\n",
    "        markerfacecolor = \"red\",\n",
    "        markersize = 10\n",
    "       )\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Sales VS Profit\")\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"X\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Y\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.grid()\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b2b9c815-4272-46ce-b8ea-f02b69ac44d6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Figure Size"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "768f640e-07e3-4f19-81dc-404b3c4833e3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Why change the figure size?\n",
    "Matplotlib chooses a default chart size.\n",
    "    \n",
    "In real work, we often change the size so the chart is:\n",
    "- easier to read\n",
    "- suitable for a report\n",
    "- suitable for a presentation\n",
    "- not too small or too large\n",
    "\n",
    "syntax = fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 6))"
   ]
  },
  {